e class as,\nL435@P14: the H Shares in issue on the relevant registration date, except\nL436@P14: for any right excluded by mandatory provisions of applicable\nL437@P14: law.\nL438@P14: Redemption at Maturity: Unless previously redeemed, converted or purchased\nL439@P14: and cancelled as provided in the Terms and Conditions,\nL529@P16: 5.36% of the number of Shares in issue as enlarged by the issue of the Conversion Shares\nL530@P16: upon the full conversion of the Bonds. The Conversion Shares will be fully-paid and rank pari\nL531@P16: passu in all respects with the H Shares then in issue on the relevant registration date, except\nL532@P16: for any right excluded by mandatory provisions of applicable law.\nL533@P16: Application for Listing\nL534@P16: The Company will make or cause to be made an application for the Bonds to be listed on the\nL542@P17: As completion of the Subscription is subject to the satisfaction of certain conditions\nL543@P17: precedent and the termination rights of the Managers, the Bonds may or may not be\nL544@P17: issued and/or the Conversion Shares may or may not be issued or listed. Shareholders\nL545@P17: and potential investors of the Company are advised to exercise caution when dealing in\nL546@P17: the securities of the Company.\nL547@P17: GENERAL MANDATE FOR ISSUANCE OF THE PLACING SHARES AND THE\nL548@P17: CONVERSION SHARES\nL549@P17: The Placing Shares to be issued and allotted and the Conversion Shares to be issued and\nL550@P17: allotted upon conversion of the Bonds will be issued by the Company under the General\nL551@P17: Mandate, pursuant to which the Board is authorized to allot, issue and deal with up to\nL552@P17: 89,168,618 Shares (including securities convertible into such Shares), equivalent to 20% of\nL553@P17: the 445,843,090 Shares in issue as at the date of the annual general meeting of the Company\nL554@P17: held on June 22, 2026.\nL555@P17: As at the date of this announcement, 19,780,000 Shares have been allotted and issued under\nL556@P17: the General Mandate pursuant to the First Placing, and no further Shares have been allotted\nL557@P17: and issued under the General Mandate. The Board has approved the Placing and the issue of\nL558@P17: the Bonds under the General Mandate, and the placing and issue of the Placing Shares, the issue\nL559@P17: of the Bonds and the allotment and issuance of the Conversion Shares are therefore not subject\nL560@P17: to the Shareholders’ further approval.\nL561@P17: EQUITY FINANCING ACTIVITIES IN THE PAST 12 MONTHS\nL562@P17: On January 8, 2026, the Company issued 37,419,500 new H Shares at HK$116.20 per H\nL563@P17: Share. On February 4, 2026, as part of the Global Offering, the over-allotment option was\nL564@P17: fully exercised and the Company issued additional 5,623,900 H Shares at HK$116.20 per H\nL565@P17: Shares. The total net proceeds from the Global Offering (including the exercise of the over\u0002allotment option) was approximately HK$4,896.2 million. (the “IPO Proceeds”). As of\nL566@P17: August 31, 2026, the IPO Proceeds had been fully utilized in accordance with the intended uses\nL567@P17: set out in the Prospectus.\nL568@P17: On July 9, 2026, the Company entered into a placing agreement in relation to the placing\nL569@P17: of up to 19,780,000 new H Shares under the General Mandate (the “First Placing”), details\nL570@P17: of which were set out in the announcement of the Company dated July 9, 2026 (the “First\nL571@P17: Placing Announcement”). Completion of the First Placing took place on July 13, 2026,\nL572@P17: pursuant to which an aggregate of 19,780,000 new H Shares were allotted and issued at a\nL573@P17: placing price of HK$1,588.00 per H Share, representing approximately 4.25% of the total\nL574@P17: number of H Shares in issue as enlarged by the allotment and issue of such shares. The\nL575@P17: aggregate net proceeds from the First Placing (after deducting commission and estimated\nL576@P17: expenses) were approximately HK$31,374.95 million (the “First Placing Proceeds”), details\nL577@P17-18: of which were set out in the completion announcement of the Company dated July 13, 2026 – 19 –\nL578@P18: (together with the First Placing Announcement, the “First Placing Announcements”).\nL579@P18: As of August 31, 2026, the Company had utilized approximately HK$10,954.80 million,\nL580@P18: representing approximately 34.92% of the First Placing Proceeds, in accordance with the\nL581@P18: intended uses set out in the First Placing Announcements. The unutilized portion of the First\nL582@P18: Placing Proceeds amounted to approximately HK$20,420.15 million (the “Unutilized First\nL583@P18: Placing Proceeds”). The Company intends to continue to utilize the Unutilized First Placing\nL584@P18: Proceeds in accordance with the intended uses and the corresponding allocation as disclosed\nL585@P18: in the First Placing Announcements.\nL586@P18: Save as disclosed above, the Company had no financing activities involving issuance of equity\nL587@P18: securities in the 12 months immediately prior to the date of this announcement.\nL588@P18: REASONS FOR AND BENEFITS OF THE PLACING AND THE ISSUE OF THE\nL589@P18: BONDS\nL590@P18: The Company is a leading AI company in China, dedicated to developing general-purpose\nL591@P18: large models and committed to a full-stack indigenous innovation technology approach. As the\nL592@P18: Company continues to advance the research and development (“R&D”) of its next-generation\nL593@P18: General Language Model (GLM) foundation models, its Fully Self Training system and\nL594@P18: long-horizon task reinforcement learning, and as demand for its Model-as-a Service (MaaS)\nL595@P18: platform continues to grow, the Company’s requirements for training and inference computing\nL596@P18: resources have correspondingly increased. The Company considers that quality computing\nL597@P18: resources currently offer favourable supply and delivery conditions in the market, and given\nL598@P18: the lead time required from contracting to deployment, completing its financing arrangements\nL599@P18: at this stage will help align the pace of deployment of additional computing capacity with its\nL600@P18: expansion plans.\nL601@P18: As of August 31, 2026, the IPO Proceeds had been fully utilized, and approximately 34.92%\nL602@P18: of the First Placing Proceeds had been utilized, primarily to support the Company’s established\nL603@P18: development strategy and business expansion, in accordance with the intended uses as set\nL604@P18: out in the Prospectus and the First Placing Announcements, respectively. As the Company’s\nL605@P18: business has progressed and accelerated, the pace of utilization of proceeds under the original\nL606@P18: fundraising plan has correspondingly increased. Having given careful consideration, and\nL607@P18: having regard to the Company’s current cash position and the continuing trend of front-loaded\nL608@P18: investment in model iteration and computing power, the Directors are of the view that the\nL609@P18: introduction of additional capital through the Placing and the issue of the Bonds will further\nL610@P18: strengthen the Company’s capital position and support its continued pursuit of foundation\nL611@P18: model research and development, technological innovation, commercialisation and ecosystem\nL612@P18: building.\nL613@P18: The Directors are of the view that, in light of the current market environment, the Placing and\nL614@P18: the issue of the Bonds represent both an opportune and appropriate financing arrangement for\nL615@P18-19: the Company. The Placing and the issue of the Bonds will assist in raising additional capital – 20 –\nL616@P19: to support the business growth and development of the Group, and will further optimize\nL617@P19: the Company’s shareholder structure and capital base. After considering various factors,\nL618@P19: including but not limited to current market conditions, the Board is of the view that the terms\nL619@P19: of the Placing Agreement and the Subscription Agreement (including, but not limited to, the\nL620@P19: Placing Price, the Conversion Price and the commission and fees payable to the Joint Placing\nL621@P19: Agents and the Managers) are fair and reasonable and in the interest of the Company and its\nL622@P19: Shareholders as a whole.\nL623@P19: USE OF PROCEEDS\nL624@P19: Assuming that the total number of Placing Shares is placed to the Placees in full, the total\nL625@P19: gross proceeds from the Placing are expected to be approximately HK$15,683.01 million, and\nL626@P19: the net proceeds (after deducting commission and estimated expenses) from the Placing are\nL627@P19: expected to be approximately HK$15,664.13 million in aggregate.\nL628@P19: Subject to completion of the Subscription, the total gross proceeds from the issue of the\nL629@P19: Bonds are expected to be approximately US$3,015.64 million (equivalent to approximately\nL630@P19: HK$23,648.44 million), and the net proceeds (after deducting the Managers’ commissions\nL631@P19: and other estimated expenses) from the issue of the Bonds are expected to be approximately\nL632@P19: US$3,010.77 million (equivalent to approximately HK$23,610.24 million), representing a net\nL633@P19: issue price of approximately HK$895.51 per Conversion Share based on the initial Conversion\nL634@P19: Price (subject to adjustments).\nL635@P19: The Company is conducting the Placing and the issue of the Bonds with the aim of further\nL636@P19: broadening its shareholder equity base, seizing the development opportunities presented by\nL637@P19: the evolution of general-purpose artificial intelligence from model invocation towards long\u0002horizon tasks and end-to-end task delivery, providing adequate financial support for the R&D,\nL638@P19: training and inference infrastructure deployment of next-generation models and the scale-up of\nL639@P19: commercialization, and ensuring the Group’s long-term, stable and sustainable development.\nL640@P19: The Company intends to use the proceeds from the Placing and the issue of the Bonds for the\nL641@P19: purposes and in the amounts as set forth below:\nL642@P19: (a) Approximately 60% of the net proceeds will be used for the R&D of the Company’s\nL643@P19: next-generation GLM foundation models and its Fully Self Training system, as\nL644@P19: well as the deployment and upgrade of large-scale training, production inference,\nL645@P19: computing resources and related technology infrastructure, with the objective of\nL646@P19: continuously enhancing the models’ intelligence ceiling, long-horizon task capability,\nL647@P19: self-improvement capability, iteration efficiency and scaled service capability. The\nL648@P19: Company’s R&D and infrastructure investment to be funded by the proceeds will\nL649@P19: principally focus on the following areas:\nL650@P19: (i) Continuous iteration of next-generation foundation models. The Company intends\nL651@P19: to continue the R&D and version iteration of its next-generation GLM foundation\nL652@P19: models, focusing on the key determinants of model capability, with continued\nL653@P19-20: investment in the following directions:– 21 –\nL654@P20: – Foundation scale and native capability. The Company intends to increase the\nL655@P20: effective scale, native context length and native multimodal unified modelling\nL656@P20: capability of its foundation models, enabling the models to accommodate a\nL657@P20: higher density of knowledge and more complex task structures and providing\nL658@P20: a higher technical ceiling for subsequent capability improvements.\nL659@P20: – Effective depth and long-horizon reasoning. The Company intends to explore\nL660@P20: ways to increase effective computational depth without disproportionately\nL661@P20: increasing model activation scale or inference cost, enabling the models to\nL662@P20: perform longer chains of reasoning, planning and self-verification, so as to\nL663@P20: improve goal consistency and execution stability in complex tasks.\nL664@P20: – Training depth and reinforcement learning. The Company intends to continue\nL665@P20: investing across the pre-training, mid-training and post-training stages of\nL666@P20: model development based on the marginal returns of each stage, expanding\nL667@P20: the scale of long-horizon task reinforcement learning and effective training\nL668@P20: trajectories, and optimizing reward allocation, feedback utilization and\nL669@P20: continual learning mechanisms, so as to fully unlock the capabilities of its\nL670@P20: foundation models.\nL671@P20: – Long-horizon task environments and agent capability. The Company intends\nL672@P20: to build executable, verifiable task environments that closely resemble real\u0002world professional work, training the models’ task decomposition, tool use,\nL673@P20: environment interaction, error recovery and result verification capabilities,\nL674@P20: and exploring the evolution of agent working modes and the enhancement of\nL675@P20: execution capability.\nL676@P20: (ii) Fully Self Training system. The Company intends to explore a technical loop in\nL677@P20: which the models participate in building and improving their own training systems,\nL678@P20: progressively increasing the degree of automation of data, task environments and\nL679@P20: infrastructure. Related R&D will principally cover the following directions:\nL680@P20: – Data self-generation. The Company intends to generate, curate and\nL681@P20: accumulate high-quality data through model-to-model self-play, rule-based\nL682@P20: verification, execution verification, model review and manual spot-checking,\nL683@P20: so that verifiable, executable and reviewable data can continuously flow back\nL684@P20: into the pre-training, mid-training and post-training stages.\nL685@P20: – Task-environment self-generation. The Company intends to develop technical\nL686@P20: processes for agents to collect and convert real-world tasks, attempt tasks,\nL687@P20: generate verifiers and check task solvability, and to continuously expand\nL688@P20: the number, variety and complexity of training environments, so that task\nL689@P20-21: environments can become a scalable and reusable training resource.– 22 –\nL690@P21: – Infrastructure self-optimization. The Company intends to leverage the\nL691@P21: models’ capabilities in coding and systems engineering to assist in developing\nL692@P21: and optimizing the operators, kernels, scheduling, caching and serving stacks\nL693@P21: of its training and inference systems, enabling the models to progressively\nL694@P21: participate in upgrading the infrastructure that supports their own iteration.\nL695@P21: (iii) Training, inference and computing infrastructure. The Company intends to deploy\nL786@P23: management, where appropriate, and (vi) other general corporate purposes consistent\nL787@P23: with the Company’s ordinary course of business and long-term development strategy.\nL788@P23: The Company intends to utilize the net proceeds from the Placing and the issue of the Bonds\nL789@P23: for the above intended uses and expects the net proceeds from the Placing and the issue of the\nL790@P23: Bonds to be fully utilized by June 30, 2028.\nL791@P23: To the extent that the net proceeds from the Placing and the issue of the Bonds are not\nL803@P24: completion of the Placing and the issue and allotment of the Conversion Shares assuming full\nL804@P24: conversion of the Bonds at the initial Conversion Price of HK$892.50 (subject to adjustments),\nL805@P24: in each case assuming that the Placing Shares are fully placed and except for the issue of\nL806@P24: Placing Shares and the issue of the Conversion Shares upon full conversion of the Bonds at\nL807@P24: the initial Conversion Price of HK$892.50 (subject to adjustments), there is no change in the\nL930@P27: 於加強境內企業境外發行證券和上市相關保密和檔案管理\nL931@P27: 工作的規定》) issued by the CSRC effective from March 31,\nL932@P27: 2023, as amended, supplemented or otherwise modified from\nL933@P27: time to time\nL934@P27: “Director(s)” director(s) of the Company\nL935@P27: “Fully Self Training” the Group’s technical vision that the next generation of\nL936@P27: GLM models will be trained in environments built by the\nL937@P27: previous generation of GLM models, forming a closed\nL938@P27: loop of Recursive Self-Improvement, encompassing three\nL939@P27: dimensions: self-generated data, self-built environments, and\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www1.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2026/0913/2026091300025.pdf)\nciteturn775view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 31; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn774view0\",\"pattern\":\"60%\"}); Total lines: 1044\nL216@P6-7: agreement that transfers, in whole or in part, the economic risk of ownership of such Shares, – 8 –\nL217@P7: whether any such transaction described in (i) or (ii) above is to be settled by delivery of\nL218@P7: Shares or such other securities, in cash or otherwise, or (iii) publicly announce an intention to\nL219@P7: effect any such transaction, for a period beginning on the date of the Placing Agreement and\nL220@P7: ending on the date which is 60 days after the Closing Date. The foregoing shall not apply to\nL221@P7: (a) the issue of the Placing Shares, (b) the issue of the Bonds and the issue of any H Shares\nL222@P7: pursuant to the exercise of the conversion rights attaching to the Bonds, and (c) the allotment\nL223@P7: and issuance of any Shares or the grant of equity-based awards pursuant to the terms of\nL224@P7: 2026 share award scheme of the Company adopted on June 22, 2026 in compliance with the\nL225@P7: applicable requirements of the Listing Rules from time to time.\nL342@P11: be expected to, result in any of the aforesaid (whether by actual disposition or effective\nL343@P11: 