eds from the Placing and the issue of the Bonds for the\nL641@P19: purposes and in the amounts as set forth below:\nL642@P19: (a) Approximately 60% of the net proceeds will be used for the R&D of the Company’s\nL643@P19: next-generation GLM foundation models and its Fully Self Training system, as\nL644@P19: well as the deployment and upgrade of large-scale training, production inference,\nL645@P19: computing resources and related technology infrastructure, with the objective of\nL646@P19: continuously enhancing the models’ intelligence ceiling, long-horizon task capability,\nL647@P19: self-improvement capability, iteration efficiency and scaled service capability. The\nL648@P19: Company’s R&D and infrastructure investment to be funded by the proceeds will\nL649@P19: principally focus on the following areas:\nL650@P19: (i) Continuous iteration of next-generation foundation models. The Company intends\nL651@P19: to continue the R&D and version iteration of its next-generation GLM foundation\nL652@P19: models, focusing on the key determinants of model capability, with continued\nL653@P19-20: investment in the following directions:– 21 –\nL654@P20: – Foundation scale and native capability. The Company intends to increase the\nL655@P20: effective scale, native context length and native multimodal unified modelling\nL656@P20: capability of its foundation models, enabling the models to accommodate a\nL657@P20: higher density of knowledge and more complex task structures and providing\nL658@P20: a higher technical ceiling for subsequent capability improvements.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www1.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2026/0913/2026091300025.pdf)\nciteturn775view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 31; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn774view0\",\"pattern\":\"September 13\"}); Total lines: 1044\nL1030@P30: “U.S. Dollar Equivalent” in respect of a Renminbi-denominated amount due under the\nL1031@P30: Bonds, the U.S. dollars amount converted from the relevant\nL1032@P30: Renminbi amount pursuant to the Terms and Conditions\nL1033@P30: “U.S. Securities Act” United States Securities Act of 1933, as amended\nL1034@P30: “%” per cent\nL1035@P30: By order of the Board\nL1036@P30: Z.AI Co., Ltd.\nL1037@P30: Dr. LIU Debing\nL1038@P30: Executive Director and Chairman of the Board\nL1039@P30: Hong Kong, September 13, 2026\nL1040@P30: As at the date of this announcement, the Board comprises: (i) Dr. Liu Debing, Dr. Zhang\nL1041@P30: Peng and Ms. Zhang Xiaohan as executive Directors; (ii) Dr. Li Juanzi, Mr. Li Jiaqing and\nL1042@P30: Mr. Wang Meng as non-executive Directors; and (iii) Dr. Yang Qiang, Dr. Xie Deren and\nL1043@P30: Mr. Xu Wenming as independent non-executive Directors.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www1.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2026/0913/2026091300025.pdf)\nciteturn775view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 31; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn774view0\",\"pattern\":\"September 16\"}); Total lines: 1044\nL193@P6: (b) the Joint Placing Agents having received on the Closing Date (as defined below) the\nL194@P6: relevant legal opinions and other documentation as set out in the Placing Agreement.\nL195@P6: Save for condition (a) above, the Joint Placing Agents shall have the sole discretion to waive\nL196@P6: the other conditions for the Placing as set out above.\nL197@P6: Completion of the Placing\nL198@P6: Subject to the satisfaction or waiver of the conditions of the Placing, the completion of the\nL199@P6: Placing shall take place on September 16, 2026 or such other time and/or date as the Company\nL200@P6: and the Joint Placing Agents agree in writing (the “Closing Date”).\nL201@P6: Application for Listing\nL202@P6: The Company will apply to the Listing Committee for listing of, and permission 